.SS "enum \fBSystemEx\&.CompareResult\fP : sbyte"

.PP
Specifies the result of a comparison between two values\&. This enumeration is used by CompFunc<T> and the generic algorithms in Algorithm to express ordering relations between two operands \fRA\fP and \fRB\fP\&. It generalizes the usual "less/greater/equal" semantics with additional states for "equal butsmaller" and "equal but larger" to support nuanced ordering logic\&. 
.PP
\fBEnumerator\fP
.in +1c
.TP
\f(BILess \fP
Alias for \fBCompareResult\&.AIsSmallerB\fP\&. Indicates that the first operand is strictly smaller than the second\&. 
.TP
\f(BIGreater \fP
Alias for \fBCompareResult\&.AIsLargerB\fP\&. Indicates that the first operand is strictly larger than the second\&. 
.TP
\f(BIEqualLess \fP
Alias for \fBCompareResult\&.AIsEqualSmallerB\fP\&. Indicates that the first operand is equal to the second but considered "smaller" in a secondary ordering dimension\&. 
.TP
\f(BIEqualGreater \fP
Alias for \fBCompareResult\&.AIsEqualLargerB\fP\&. Indicates that the first operand is equal to the second but considered "larger" in a secondary ordering dimension\&. 
.TP
\f(BIAIsLargerB \fP
The first operand \fRA\fP is strictly larger than the second operand \fRB\fP\&. 
.TP
\f(BIAIsSmallerB \fP
The first operand \fRA\fP is strictly smaller than the second operand \fRB\fP\&. 
.TP
\f(BIEqual \fP
The operands \fRA\fP and \fRB\fP are considered equal in the primary ordering dimension\&. 
.TP
\f(BIAIsEqualLargerB \fP
The operands are equal in the primary dimension, but \fRA\fP is treated as "greater" in a secondary dimension (e\&.g\&. tie‑breaking)\&. 
.TP
\f(BIAIsEqualSmallerB \fP
The operands are equal in the primary dimension, but \fRA\fP is treated as "smaller" in a secondary dimension\&. 
.TP
\f(BINull \fP
One or both operands are \fRnull\fP, or the comparison function cannot produce a meaningful ordering result\&. 
.PP
